  "title": "OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al. 2019)",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted derivative dataset of steady-state visually evoked potential (SSVEP) EEG recordings from 54 subjects across 2 sessions. This dataset comprises 21,600 trials of 4-second EEG recordings sampled at 1000 Hz from 62 channels, designed for brain-computer interface benchmarking using a 4-class SSVEP paradigm. The data has been standardized and organized using the Mother of All BCI Benchmarks (MOABB) framework to facilitate reproducible analysis and comparison of BCI algorithms.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were collected using a 62-channel montage at 1000 Hz sampling frequency across 2 sessions with 4-second trial durations in a 4-class SSVEP paradigm. Detailed acquisition and experimental protocols are described in the primary publication (DOI: 10.1093/gigascience/giz002).",
